WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
A young man in a long coat walks
a path lined with doorways.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.320
Above one door, a word lights up: Destiny.

3
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.370
Above another: Fate.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.270
Then: Angel of Destruction.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.050
Above the other doors, nothing lights up.

6
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.280
So what moves him through those?

7
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.640
Victor Frankenstein tells
us: "Destiny was too potent".

8
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.570
Should we take his word for it?

9
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.200
In this mission, you'll
follow Victor's path,

10
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.860
from a loved childhood in
Geneva to the Arctic ice.

11
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.140
You'll keep in mind who is telling it.

12
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.460
Victor narrates most of the novel,
so we mostly see events his way.

13
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.110
And you'll collect the words he uses
to blame something bigger than himself.

14
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.620
Your mission: decide whether to
believe Victor when he blames destiny.
